WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.605
Every PowerPoint to video converter makes different trade-offs.

2
00:00:04.655 --> 00:00:09.064
Before you pick one, ask the right questions, so the tool fits your work.

3
00:00:09.564 --> 00:00:12.010
Start with the job the video must do.

4
00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:19.105
Who's watching, where it will live, how often it changes, and how sensitive the content is will decide most things.

5
00:00:19.964 --> 00:00:23.362
Next, narration: record it or write it.

6
00:00:23.412 --> 00:00:31.503
If your deck changes often, narration from your speaker notes is easier, because fixing a sentence means editing text, not re-recording.

7
00:00:32.003 --> 00:00:36.457
For sensitive material, check your organisation's policy before uploading.

8
00:00:36.507 --> 00:00:42.763
Then preview a real deck, not a demo, and ask: does it improve your story, or just play it back?

9
00:00:43.403 --> 00:00:52.828
Look for timing that follows the speech, captions for viewers with the sound off, an MP4 your platform accepts, and clear limits on price and watermarks.

10
00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:57.387
Ordinary slides in, extraordinary video out.

11
00:00:57.437 --> 00:01:03.250
Try it first on Basic, no subscription needed, or go Pro and let a.i. direct it.

12
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.713
Visit powerpoint2vid.com.

